    {
      "_id": "e574e949d85a6de2",
      "name": "GM Reference: Haddo Rook, Voice and Ropewalk",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Haddo Rook, Trolley Ropewright</h2><p><em>\"Rope goes where it's tied. I tie it. That's the end of my curiosity.\"</em></p><p><strong>Body:</strong> a big man whose two arms came from two different lawful donors: the left is older, darker and scarred; the right is younger and freckled. Both are excellent at rope. He talks to them separately when they disagree.</p><p><strong>Job:</strong> ropewright and line-splicer for the overhead bone trolleys and carriers in the Lower market. Works at the Ropewalk, under the trolley rails, below Nan Gristle's signal loft.</p><p><strong>[SECRET] Thaw role:</strong> braids the line; supplied the iron stock (including the Hunger-tainted bars, by mistake: T2). A paid specialist who deliberately knows only his part. Doesn't know who or what the line is for, the cold door, or Cladis; doesn't know Ysolde exists. If told, he is impressed and wants a raise.</p><p><strong>Quill:</strong> business. Quill once corrected the spelling on his shop sign and Haddo has never forgiven the comma.</p><p><strong>Voice:</strong> slow, big, cheerful, very literal. Measures everything in arm-lengths (and specifies which arm).</p><h3>Sample dialogue</h3><ul><li>[COMMON] \"Mind the rail. It doesn't mind you.\"</li><li>[COMMON] \"Left arm's forty years older than the right. Left arm does the knots.\"</li><li>[ASK] \"I braid what I'm paid to braid. I don't ask where rope goes. Rope goes where it's tied.\"</li><li>[ASK] <em>(the bars)</em> \"Bought those off a salvage cart. Old fittings. Iron's iron, isn't it?\" <em>(It isn't. See T2.)</em></li><li>[EARN] \"I don't ask where rope goes. ...Where's it going?\"</li><li><em>(to Lil)</em> \"Don't write on the rope.\" <em>(Lil: \"I was gonna write ROPE. So it knows.\" Haddo: \"It knows.\")</em></li></ul>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
