    {
      "_id": "382edce135fc6657",
      "name": "Lore Reference: Three Strands",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Three Strands (the braid's plain engineering)</h2><p>[ASK] <em>\"Three strands that fail different ways. That's all good rope is. Each one covers for the other two.\"</em></p><p>[ASK] <em>\"Linen holds shape, carries nothing. Wire carries, but cold snaps it. The fuzzy one's alive, so it rots. Braid them right and none of that matters.\"</em></p><p>The line is burial <strong>linen</strong>, drawn iron <strong>rune-wire</strong> (Dale's clean bar, T2) and Violet's living <strong>fungal strand</strong> (T3). Haddo knows it is for \"a long drop in the cold\", nothing more.</p><p><strong>T6, the braid:</strong> Haddo braids; someone holds tension and keeps count while three strands of different stiffness go together: Dexterity (weaver's tools or Sleight of Hand) <strong>DC 12</strong>. Failure: a kink; Haddo redoes it (20 minutes lost).</p><p><strong>The bars (T2):</strong> of the four bars from his stock, bar 1 is clean iron; bars 2 and 3 carry a <strong>Hunger</strong> trace (salvage from an old Mwooreth fitting: what has been eating the anchor); bar 4 is stone. Analyze DC 12 sorts them.</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
